-- title:
--   Cylinder ratios at the similarity exponent sum to one
-- statement:
--   A self-similar system on the line consists of finitely many maps $f_i(x)=r_ix+b_i$ with $0<|r_i|<1$ and weights $w_i>0$ summing to $1$; a probability measure $\mu$ is self-similar when $\mu=\sum_iw_i(f_i)_*\mu$. The coding map sends an address $\omega\in\iota^{\mathbb N}$ to $\pi(\omega)=\lim_nf_{\omega_0}\circ\cdots\circ f_{\omega_{n-1}}(0)$, and the system has no exact overlaps when distinct finite words give distinct composed maps. If $s\ge0$ and $\sum_i|r_i|^s=1$, then for every $n$,
--   $$
--   \sum_{|w|=n}\Bigl(\prod_j|r_{w_j}|\Bigr)^s=1 .
--   $$
--
--   This exact partition-function identity holds whether or not cylinders overlap.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MeasureTheory/SelfSimilar/Attractor.lean#L80-L100

